HST Office on Windows: own class IDs for its Explorer extensions and search filter.

HST's shlxthdl.dll, propertyhdl.dll and ooofilt.dll used LibreOffice's class IDs: the infotip,
column, property sheet and thumbnail handlers, the property handler, the indexing filter and its
persistent handler. With both suites installed, HKCR\CLSID\{...}\InprocServer32 pointed to the DLL
of the suite installed last, and uninstalling either deleted the class registration, so the other
lost thumbnails, infotips, the Details pane properties and search of ODF content.

- New class IDs in the code (shell/inc/shlxthdl.hxx, propertyhdl.hxx, ooofilt.hxx) and in every
  scp2 entry (CLSID keys, Shell Extensions\Approved, ColumnHandlers, PropertySheetHandlers,
  PersistentHandler, PropertyHandlers):
    infotip         {087B3AE3-E237-4467-B8DB-5A38AB959AC9} -> {2A30C089-4A9F-4456-9E48-AEB9FF0012A3}
    column          {C52AF81D-F7A0-4AAB-8E87-F80A60CCD396} -> {0643B6EE-B40D-4AA5-AC91-6849F83692BD}
    property sheet  {63542C48-9552-494A-84F7-73AA6A7C99C1} -> {9A9E8777-D20C-40AD-826C-085F05B40FA6}
    thumbnail       {3B092F0C-7696-40E3-A80F-68D74DA84210} -> {BC84498F-C467-4BD6-9876-D44924DA54D0}
    property        {AE424E85-F6DF-4910-A6A9-438797986431} -> {A5B95EEC-7757-43B4-A663-634CF2E9A67A}
    filter          {7BC0E710-5703-45BE-A29D-5D46D8B39262} -> {A0914CEA-1A1D-4B82-A200-FE2818319A03}
    persistent      {7BC0E713-5703-45BE-A29D-5D46D8B39262} -> {11AF517D-5B69-4366-92C2-C1C3B7493418}
- The infotip and thumbnail handlers are attached to HST's own ProgIDs (HSTOffice.*\shellex)
  instead of the shared .odt/.ods/... extension keys, so HST no longer overwrites or deletes the
  handlers LibreOffice attaches to those extensions. Windows only reads the search persistent
  handler and the property handler per extension; these stay on the extension, where the last
  installer wins (like the .odt default).
- Unchanged on purpose: the OLE embedding class IDs (documents store them) and Microsoft's
  interface IDs (IFilter, IQueryInfo, IExtractImage).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

